# USER - Select a numbered user area

```text
USER number
```

## Change user

```text
USER 3
DIR
USER 0
```

USER selects a number from 0 through 31 on the current drive. The prompt
shows the new location. Files in other user areas remain on the disk.

## Work elsewhere

A numeric prefix lets you access another location without changing the
prompt. DIR D3:*.TXT lists text files in user 3 of D. [NDR](NDR.HLP)
lets you name a frequently used drive/user.
